Industrial Camera Linux Driver Installation and Uninstallation Guide  
===========================================================================

Driver Installation and Uninstallation:  
===========================================================================  
(1) After installing the client, the drivers are located in the `/opt/(software name)/driver` directory.  
(2) Driver Installation: The installation method is the same for both GigE and PCIe drivers. The `gige` folder contains the filter driver, while the `pcie` folder contains the frame grabber driver. First, navigate to the `gige` or `pcie` directory, execute `sudo bash build.sh`, and then run `sudo bash load.sh`.  
(3) Driver Uninstallation: The uninstallation method is the same for both GigE and PCIe drivers. First, navigate to the `gige` or `pcie` directory and execute `sudo bash unload.sh`.  
===========================================================================

Method to Check if the Installation is Successful:  
===========================================================================  
(1) Execute the `lsmod` command and check if the following modules are present:  
    Modules:  
    ├── gevfilter (Filter Driver)  
    ├── gevframegrabber (GigE Frame Grabber Driver)  
    ├── cxpframegrabber (CXP Frame Grabber Driver)  
    ├── cmlframegrabber (CML Frame Grabber Driver)  
    ├── xofframegrabber (XOF Frame Grabber Driver)  
    └── lightcontroller (Light Controller Driver)